  "summary": "Four recent preprints fold motif diversity, single-cell dynamics, replicate variability and ODE parameter structure into the inference step itself.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is that structure is encoded inside the optimization or inference objective rather than applied afterward. MAP-Elites reframes PWM motif discovery as quality-diversity search on human liver CTCF ChIP-seq data, recovering diverse high-fitness motifs. WFR-MFM uses mean-flow unbalanced optimal transport to perform one-step inference of single-cell dynamics, reported as faster than trajectory-simulation baselines. A robust product-of-experts formulation pools highly variable empirical replicates for collective simulation-based posterior inference. eLSHADE+ applies adaptive multi-strategy differential evolution to ODE parameter estimation, outperforming eSS on BioPreDyn. What is new is treating motif diversity, dynamics, replicate variability, and ODE parameter estimation as explicit components of the model.",
